.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KUBE-SMOKE-TEST 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kube-smoke-test
.Nd check every layer a kldload Kubernetes node depends on, and the cluster when there is one
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
checks, in order: the package manager; the kernel modules Kubernetes
needs, loading any that are not; forwarding and bridge sysctls; swap;
containerd and its cgroup driver; kubeadm, kubelet, kubectl, helm and the
Cilium CLI; the CNI plugins; ZFS and the datasets for etcd, containerd and
the kubelet; WireGuard; the firewall; images loaded for offline use; and,
when a cluster answers, its nodes, system pods, cluster DNS \(em by
starting a pod that resolves
.Ql kubernetes.default
\(em and the web console's tools.
Each check prints PASS, FAIL, WARN or SKIP, and a count ends the run.
.Pp
Each run appends its counts to
.Pa /root/kube-smoke-test.log .
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Xr kube-cluster 8
runs it on the control plane at the end of a bootstrap.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the description and exit 0, without root.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /root/kube-smoke-test.log
One line a run:
.Ql # Ar time Ns Li "  pass=" Ns Ar n Li fail= Ns Ar n Li warn= Ns Ar n ,
moved to
.Pa .old
past 2 MB.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when nothing failed; 1 when anything did.
Warnings do not count.
.Sh EXAMPLES
In a Fedora 44 container with none of Kubernetes installed, whose
complaints that it has no
.Xr lsmod 8
are left out:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kube-smoke-test
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  kldload Kubernetes Smoke Test
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

=== Package Manager ===
  PASS  dnf available

=== Kernel Modules ===
  PASS  overlay loaded
  PASS  br_netfilter loaded
  PASS  ip_vs loaded
\&...
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Smoke Test Results
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  PASS: 9
  FAIL: 6
  WARN: 11

  6 critical failures — fix before proceeding.
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Pp
The modules pass because a container shares the host's kernel.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
.Xr kube-network 8 ,
.Xr kube-status 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: the firewall checks read a large
ruleset as
.Dq No nftables rules loaded
\(em a 160 KB one, 200 times in 200 \(em and it exited with the number of
failures rather than 1.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
It is not read-only: it loads missing kernel modules, among them
.Ql br_netfilter ,
which sends bridged traffic through the firewall; and with a cluster up
it starts and deletes test pods.
Run it on a Kubernetes node, not on the host its virtual machines run on.
